    "projects": {
        "5post_crm": {
            "name": "5post_crm",
            "title": "5 Post – Parcel Locker Control System",
            "description": "Research / Visual Design, UX Design",
            "preview": 0,
            "default": 1,
            "images": [
                "./src/images/articles/5post/post_crm_0.png",
                "./src/images/articles/5post/post_crm_1.png",
                "./src/images/articles/5post/post_crm_2.png",
                "./src/images/articles/5post/post_crm_3.png"
            ],
            "video": "./src/videos/5post/preview.mp4",
            "customer": [
                "Project",
                "Fivepost, Enterprise, RU"
            ],
            "type": "enterprise",
            "links": [
                {
                    "name": "fivepost.ru",
                    "href": "https://fivepost.ru"
                }],
            "text": [
                "<div><h3>About tool</h3>\n Admin panel for managing and monitoring checkpoint cells and orders. Includes various modules for managing and monitoring devices, the technical conditions, database, etc. </div>",
                "<img src=\"./src/images/articles/5post/design_system.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">",
                "<div><h3>Application functionality</h3>\n<ul><li>Devices Control;</li><li>Parcel Control;</li><li>Database management;</li><li>Transactions and expenses control;</li><li>Invoice generating and tracking;</li></ul></div>",
                "<div><h3>Stakeholder report</h3>\n <img src=\"./src/images/articles/5post/report.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">",
                "<div><h3>Project results</h3>\n The Customer was highly satisfied. He left positive feedback on the Andersen website. He recommended Andersen as a good contractor for software solutions for his colleagues from other financial organizations. \n The project was delivered quickly and on time, to the customer’s full satisfaction. The resulting solution encompasses all the required financial needs.</div>"
            ],
            "footer": "Don’t hesitate to <a class='link' onclick=\"pageBuilder.rebuild('contact')\">send me an Email.</a> I’d love to hear from you."
        },
        "event_management_tool": {
            "name": "event_management_tool",
            "title": "Glenis Solutions – Event Management Tool",
            "description": "Research / Visual Design, UX Design",
            "preview": 0,
            "default": 1,
            "images": [
                "./src/images/articles/EMT/preview_0.png",
                "./src/images/articles/EMT/preview_1.png",
                "./src/images/articles/EMT/preview_2.png",
                "./src/images/articles/EMT/preview_3.png",
                "./src/images/articles/EMT/preview_4.png"
            ],
            "video": "./src/videos/EMT/preview.mp4",
            "customer": [
                "Project",
                "Glennis Solutions, Healthcare, USA"
            ],
            "links": [{
                "name": "glennissolutions.com",
                "href": "https://www.glennissolutions.com"
            }],
            "type": "enterprise",
            "text": [
                "<div><h3>Goals</h3>\n The project aims to create a modern, user-friendly event management system for senior communities. By enhancing the interface and adding a robust validation process, the system will simplify event planning and approval while boosting resident engagement.</div>",
                "<div><h3>About company</h3>\n The company provide communities for older people in which they can live comfortably, receive care, medicine, entertainment, and enjoy the interactions with other residents.</div>",
                "<div><h3>About tool</h3>\n Event management software is one way to make senior living better. \n EMT is a system with ability to create and submit events for review, used to manage event calendars for guests. Residents stay involved and active in their communities. The challenge is to modernize the user interface and add a validation process. \n Another thing it's a mobile app to expand software capabilities.</div>",
                "<div><h3>Application functionality</h3>\n<ul><li>Working with events;</li><li>Duplicate events;</li><li>Master Calendar feature;</li><li>Roll forward;</li><li>Existing features improvements;</li></ul></div>",
                "<div><h3>Design process</h3>\n <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/design_process.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Interviews</h3>\n As a part of the qualitative research, I've conducted a number of interviews with users in various roles. Both users with administrative access rights and regular system users were interviewed. <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/interviews.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Empathy map</h3>\n To highlight a number of potentially important hypotheses, I created an average system user empathy map, which helps identify the most important hypotheses that I was going to confirm with a quantitative research in the next step. <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/empathy_map.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Receiving data using google forms</h3>\n As part of quantitative research to confirm previously derived hypotheses, I conducted a quantitative research and identified the most successful solutions, which were later implemented at the prototyping stage. <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/answers.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"> <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/data.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Current Calendar Process</h3>\n <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/process.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Wireframes</h3>\n Once the list of MVP features has been approved by the stakeholders, I've started creating prototypes based on the data obtained from research. <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/wireframes.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"><img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/wireframes_2.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Styled components library</h3>\n Before starting the design phase, we created a shared design library. <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/design_system.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Visual design</h3>\n As a result of the visual design phase, a number of screens were built. This is important both for creating use cases and for developers use. In addition, some of the users who agreed to usability testing were invited to test the new application design. <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/design.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Mocks</h3>\n <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/Screens/1.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"><img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/Screens/2.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"><img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/Screens/3.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"><img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/Screens/4.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Mobile attendance</h3>\n After research, I've decided  to move some of the functionality from the main application to a mobile attendance mobile application. <img src=\"./src/images/articles/EMT/mobile_attendance.png\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\"></div>",
                "<div><h3>Project results</h3>\n The Customer was highly satisfied. He left positive feedback for Andersen. He recommended Andersen as a good contractor for software solutions for his colleagues from other financial organizations. \n The project was delivered quickly and on time, to the customer’s full satisfaction. The resulting solution encompasses all the required financial needs.</div>"
            ],
            "footer": "Don’t hesitate to <a class='link' onclick=\"pageBuilder.rebuild('contact')\">send me an Email.</a> I’d love to hear from you."
        },
